Upstream: the provider's Slice CRD (GKE TPU dynamic slicing)
Version: v1beta1 (accelerator.gke.io)

Hand-authored CRD stub sufficient for envtest-based integration tests
of InferenceReplica TPU slice provisioning. OME reads and writes Slices
unstructured (pkg/tpuslice/gke) and takes no dependency on the
provider's Go module, so there is no module to vendor the CRD from.

.spec is modeled on the provider's schema: the required fields, the
topology pattern and length, and the type enum. envtest therefore
rejects a Slice the provider's API server would reject. .status
preserves unknown fields (x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields): only
the provider writes it, and the tests write it in the provider's place.

Production correctness is NOT validated by this stub — the provider's
controllers do that on a live cluster.

To refresh: when the provider's Slice API changes, update .spec here
and pkg/tpuslice/gke (the pinned group, version and field paths) in the
same change.
